<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khu Bua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khu Bua is an archaeological site in Ratchaburi province in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, the remains of a moated town of the Dvaravati culture, flourishing from about the 7th to the 11th century. Excavations have uncovered brick stupas and temple bases decorated with stucco and terracotta figures, including foreigners and Buddhist scenes. It is one of the largest Dvaravati settlements known.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khu-bua.jpg" alt="Khu Bua" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahoerstemeier · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ku_Bua_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
